WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.330
Shenzhen to Rotterdam,
through the Suez Canal:

2
00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:07.750
about 10,000 nautical
miles, about 31 days.

3
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:12.230
Round Africa, via the Cape:
about 13,000 nautical miles,

4
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.190
about 41 days.

5
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.650
The Suez Canal carries about 10 per
cent of global trade by tonnage.

6
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:25.870
Yet by June 2024, Suez transits were
down 70 per cent on mid-December 2023.

7
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.210
Cape arrivals were up 89 per cent.

8
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.230
Why take the long way?

9
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.650
Was the canal closed for repairs?

10
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.730
In this mission, you'll map
the ocean's choke points,

11
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.770
from Hormuz to Panama.

12
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.090
Then you'll visit Hans Island,
between Canada and Greenland,

13
00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:46.070
where for decades both sides raised
flags and left whisky or aquavit.

14
00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:50.990
Your mission: explain why ships from
Shenzhen to Rotterdam took the long way.
